     1,
     "Thanks.  Definitely a bug.  I just opened an issue:\r<br>\r<br><a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1053\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1053&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465799354000&amp;usg=AOvVaw04FsDFlQq7zcBvZHvCR9bf\">https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1053</a>\r<br>\r<br>I scheduled the fix for the release after 2.5, but haven&#39;t\r<br>assigned it to anyone.  We also need to check a bunch of other\r<br>RNGs for the same issue.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Sep 29, 2014, at 1:53 AM, Soga Shota &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">soga....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>\r<br>&gt; Hi all,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I think the following code reproduces a bug in poisson_rng. this should be due to an overflow in int in stan.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; data\r<br>&gt; {\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; transformed data\r<br>&gt; {\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; parameters\r<br>&gt; {\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; transformed parameters\r<br>&gt; {\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; model\r<br>&gt; {\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; generated quantities\r<br>&gt; {\r<br>&gt;    real&lt;lower=0&gt; lambda;\r<br>&gt;    real                  x;\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;    lambda &lt;- lognormal_rng(10E10,10);\r<br>&gt;    x      &lt;- poisson_rng(lambda);\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;   if(x &lt; 0)\r<br>&gt;   {\r<br>&gt;       print(&quot;bug: &quot;, x);\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; the script to run the code is\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; ./test  sample algorithm=fixed_param num_warmup=5000 num_samples=10000 random seed=12345\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; and I got the following\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; bug: -2.14748e+09\r<br>&gt; bug: -2.14748e+09\r<br>&gt; bug: -2.14748e+09\r<br>&gt; bug: -2.14748e+09\r<br>&gt; bug: -2.14748e+09\r<br>&gt; bug: -2.14748e+09\r<br>&gt; ...\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
